{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01CMx5Vc9roK5yTdmpKLABh3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Here's what was written for **Q12: RNN vs LSTM**:\n\n**Key content:**\n- **Root cause**: Vanilla RNN's multiplicative gradient flow (`W_h` repeated multiplication) causes exponential vanishing over long sequences\n- **LSTM fix**: Additive cell-state update `c_t = f_t ⊙ c_{t-1} + i_t ⊙ g_t` — the forget gate near 1 acts as a skip connection through time, letting gradients flow without decay\n- **GRU**: Simpler variant (~33% fewer params) merging forget+input gates; comparable empirical performance\n- **2026 relevance**: Transformers have displaced LSTMs for NLP; LSTMs still win for edge/on-device streaming inference (fixed hidden-state size, no KV cache) and legacy time-series systems\n- **Comparison table**: Vanilla RNN / LSTM / GRU / Transformer across sequence length, parameters, training speed, gradient flow\n\n**Pitfalls captured**: Not explaining the vanishing-gradient *root cause* (just saying \"more memory\"), treating LSTMs as still state-of-the-art for NLP, and forgetting to mention GRU as the practical middle-ground."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":380,"cache_read_input_tokens":69817,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":380,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d2022572-5927-435e-9284-dae0986b8342","uuid":"cb1803c1-b038-4e50-9d88-984cd7485e91"}
